.TH ACCESS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
access \- check access to a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int access(const char* " path ", int " mode ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks the NUL\-terminated path using the process's real user and group IDs.
Use
.B F_OK
to test existence, or combine
.BR R_OK ,
.BR W_OK ,
and
.B X_OK
to test read, write, and execute permission.
The check follows symbolic links.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Errors include
.BR EACCES ,
.BR EFAULT ,
.BR EINVAL ,
and
.BR ENOENT .
Other Linux access errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Do not use this check as authorization for a subsequent open: the path or
permissions can change between the operations. Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR access (2)
